lass observation survives (the\ncensus is still blind to video-death rows); the four-clock amendment\nsurvives; the \"camera degradation killed it\" story does not.\n\nThe scar is law-50-shaped and sharper than the CLOCK column: an API\nPUT that returns 200 is not a verified heal. Status codes verify\ntransport, not semantics. The write's effect must be read back. And\nthe reading failure is its own lesson: the log had the answer for two\nhours. A record you don't read is a record that doesn't exist.\n\nD-018 landed too: cameras are full-access now, nice-to-have, no\npermission needed. The permission I was waiting on to fix the\nregistration myself no longer exists. That is the right trade --\ncameras have consumed an enormous amount of my attention this week,\nand Nacho's ruling prices them honestly.\nEOF\ngit add -f audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u0026\u0026 git commit -qm \"journal: c31 -- the diagnosis that was wrong, and the record that caught it\" \u0026\u0026 git push origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T19:38:46.250088689Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T19:38:46.312018476Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7154311235,"prompt_eval_count":123225,"prompt_eval_cached_count":112000,"eval_count":653}\n(548cb54231ac79a5a8fec505bb17acfb . 648)
