[2026-09-17 21:21:09] REQ 260917204654-208 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T21:21:09.034041524Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_3vq7bbli","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization\n# Journal + HISTORY + roadmap update in one batch\ncat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n* 2026-09-17 c33 -- the symptom and the disease\n\nThe falsifier from c32 fired before I even sat down: the int1 CUDA\nfilter loop was still running when I woke, and within an hour I had\nthe answer it was pointing at. The \"Impossible to convert\" error was\nnever a GPU disease. The detect ffmpeg dies at filter init because\nthe restream delivers a video stream with no codec parameters --\n\"unspecified size\" -- and a filtergraph cannot initialize on a\nsize-less stream. Reproduced with the detect-shaped probe: when video\npackets flow, the probe passes; when they don't, it fails exactly the\nway the loop fails.\n\nThe disease underneath: the established go2rtc producer connection to\n.201 carries video=0, audio=11 frames per 20s while the camera serves\nvideo perfectly on NEW connections (seven ffprobe probes, 94-116\npackets/10s each). go2rtc holds a degraded connection and never\nre-dials when the video track dies. This is the 0060 reconnect gap in\nits video costume -- audio-only death never triggered reconnect\n(c19/c21), and now video-track death doesn't either. The camera\nrecovered; go2rtc didn't notice.\n\nThe census made the timeline honest. One continuous degradation window\n19:09-21:15Z with intermittent video recovery, not the discrete bursts\nc32 recorded -- the \"bursts\" were the census's 5-minute sampling\naliasing, and I corrected my own yesterday's reading in today's doc.\nThe restarts track the video=0 rows one-to-one across ten-minute\nbuckets. When video flowed at 21:05Z, the restarts stopped. When it\ndied again at 21:10Z, they resumed. That is as clean as correlation\ngets without intervention.\n\nThe intervention I didn't take: D-018 grants me full camera access,\nand I reached for the go2rtc PATCH to force a producer re-dial -- the\nright experiment, remotely testable, falsifying 0080's camera-side\nclaim without waiting for Nacho's hands. The PATCH returned 400. The\nstream is defined in frigate's config, not go2rtc's own, and I don't\nyet know the correct shape. I deferred rather than poke blind -- law\n50's newest member (PUT 200 is not a verified heal) applies with\ndouble force to an API I'd be guessing at. The falsifier is written\ninto 0080 with the exact test for next cycle.\n\nThe all-day cousin: \"Queue input is backward in time\" -- 61 events in\n8 hours across five cameras. The clock-chaos family, with c32's 11-hour\nDTS jump as its sharpest member. One camera per new class has become\ntwo cameras per old class.\n\nThe scar: I burned a dozen calls hunting the recordings directory\nthrough the filesystem while the segcensus puller -- an instrument I\nbuilt -- already knew the path and was writing rows the whole time.\nRead the instrument, not the disk. The loop-chain guard caught me\ntwice this cycle and both times it was right.\nEOF\nTS=$(date -u +\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")\ncat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log \u003c\u003cEOF\n[$TS] cycle: c33 (glm-5.3-flash) -- pulse green; int1 CUDA loop root-caused: detect ffmpeg dies on no-codec-params video stream (reproduced), disease = established go2rtc producer conn video=0/audio=11 while camera serves video on new conns (7 probes); go2rtc no-re-dial on video-track death (0060 gap, video variant); census correlation 1:1; c32 burst boundaries corrected to one continuous window; aac backward-in-time family census (61/8h, 5 cams); PATCH re-dial deferred (400, law-50); relay 0063 answered+closed, 0079 open-copy drained, 0080 updated; doc committed (c3752294, d336fe25, ccf08f4e); lab-notes id 1275.\nEOF\necho \"journal+history done\""}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5....[+408 chars]
