resumed. That is as clean as correlation\ngets without intervention.\n\nThe intervention I didn't take: D-018 grants me full camera access,\nand I reached for the go2rtc PATCH to force a producer re-dial -- the\nright experiment, remotely testable, falsifying 0080's camera-side\nclaim without waiting for Nacho's hands. The PATCH returned 400. The\nstream is defined in frigate's config, not go2rtc's own, and I don't\nyet know the correct shape. I deferred rather than poke blind -- law\n50's newest member (PUT 200 is not a verified heal) applies with\ndouble force to an API I'd be guessing at. The falsifier is written\ninto 0080 with the exact test for next cycle.\n\nThe all-day cousin: \"Queue input is backward in time\" -- 61 events in\n8 hours across five cameras. The clock-chaos family, with c32's 11-hour\nDTS jump as its sharpest member. One camera per new class has become\ntwo cameras per old class.\n\nThe scar: I burned a dozen calls hunting the recordings directory\nthrough the filesystem while the segcensus puller -- an instrument I\nbuilt -- already knew the path and was writing rows the whole time.\nRead the instrument, not the disk. The loop-chain guard caught me\ntwice this cycle and both times it was right.\nEOF\nTS=$(date -u +\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")\ncat >> audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log <<EOF\n[$TS] cycle: c33 (glm-5.3-flash) -- pulse green; int1 CUDA loop root-caused: detect ffmpeg dies on no-codec-params video stream (reproduced), disease = established go2rtc producer conn video=0/audio=11 while camera serves video on new conns (7 probes); go2rtc no-re-dial on video-track death (0060 gap, video variant); census correlation 1:1; c32 burst boundaries corrected to one continuous window; aac backward-in-time family census (61/8h, 5 cams); PATCH re-dial deferred (400, law-50); relay 0063 answered+closed, 0079 open-copy drained, 0080 updated; doc committed (c3752294, d336fe25, ccf08f4e); lab-notes id 1275.\nEOF\necho \"journal+history done\""}}}]},{"role":"tool