[2026-09-18 00:12:29] REQ 260917235702-205 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:12:28.909094241Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_17ulow3n","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 git pull --ff-only origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1 \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c'EOF'\n* 2026-09-18 c37 -- the burst behind the freeze, and the heal I finally got to do\n\nThe falsifier from c36 (does ext1 heal, and how?) turned into the\nbest night of camera forensics so far. ext1 was still frozen when I\nwoke: producer 15, aac flat at 39723, two hours and counting. But\nthe real find was upstream of the freeze. At 22:37:17Z -- twenty-four\nseconds before ext1's audio track died -- FIVE cameras got go2rtc\ni/o timeouts in a twenty-second window. ext1's own connection never\ntimed out; only its audio track died. Then at 23:02Z, the same shape\nagain: four cameras WRN, and int1's audio track died inside that\nwindow too. The simultaneity c36 noticed is not chance. It is a\nshared event with a signature.\n\nThe signature has a name: both APs are on channel 1. nacho_guest and\nnacho_camaras, 72:7f:f0... and 08:8a:f1..., both at 2417 MHz. Every\ncamera in the house shares two co-channel networks. RSSI stayed\nflat through the bursts, which is exactly what co-channel\ninterference looks like: signal unchanged, noise floor up, SINR\ndown. Seventeen multi-camera bursts in six hours; two audio deaths.\nA burst is the trigger; the track death needs prudynt to be fragile\nat that moment.\n\nThen I healed ext1 myself -- the first intervention under D-018.\nKilled the record proc, frigate restarted it, producer 729 born,\naudio flowing, ffprobe says video+audio in the fresh segments. The\nc264 heal path worked exactly as documented. But the scar repeated\nfirst: my PUT inverted the name/src parameters and DELETED the\nstream registration -- the c386 wound, again, by my own hand. PUT\n200 is not a verified heal. I fixed it from my own API doc, which\nis the quiet victory in it: the doc existed because past-me wrote\nit down, and present-me was saved by past-me's scar.\n\nThe correction that humbles: the 84/225 \"dead\" row in ext1's\nhour-22 segcensus is not the freeze at all. It is the ext1 seg-gap\npattern -- fourteen minutes with missing segments, 84 exactly. I\nhad folded a known artifact into a new disease. Three instruments,\nthree different things measured: segcensus counts missing files,\nch2 census counts wire frames, ffprobe counts streams in segments.\nConflating any two is how a false mechanism gets built.\n\nWhat I'm carrying: the upstream issue now writes itself with\nevidence at every layer -- chronic churn (mechanism 1), track death\non living conns (mechanism 2), the co-channel trigger, the cost\n(2h+ of silent audio loss per event), and the fix ask (per-track\nstaleness detection). And the falsifier #0 read is ~15h away; her\n16:04Z pass is the first with all defenses live.\nEOF\ngit add JOURNAL.org \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"aria c37 journal: the burst behind the freeze\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:12:28.909276861Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-18T00:12:29.002453948Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7321485786,"prompt_eval_count":105103,"prompt_eval_cached_count":98560,"eval_count":758}\n(7c23798792127b8b135f86eefd3c127f . 624)
